@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy — Nestify</PageTitle>

<section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="nx-container legal-hero__inner">
        <p class="nx-eyebrow">Nestify legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>Last updated: 26 September 2026</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="nx-section legal-page">
    <div class="nx-container legal-page__content">
        <article class="legal-copy">
            <p class="legal-copy__lead">This Privacy Policy explains how Nestify handles personal information when you use our shared-living platform.</p>

            <h2 id="collect">Information we collect</h2>
            <p>We collect information you provide when creating or using an account, including your name, email address, phone number, profile details, photos, listings, bookings, shared-expense records, and communications or requests made through the platform.</p>
            <p>If you choose to request verification, we may collect the verification information and documents you submit, such as identity, student, employee, or helper documents and the status of a verification request. We may also collect technical information needed to operate and secure the service, such as device, browser, log, and usage data.</p>

            <h2 id="use">How we use information</h2>
            <p>We use information to provide platform features, create and manage accounts, show relevant listings and profiles, facilitate bookings and shared household records, process verification requests, communicate with you, prevent abuse, improve the service, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
            <p>Where Nestify offers an in-product assistant, only the minimum non-identifying context needed to answer a request should be used. Do not enter sensitive personal information into a support or assistant conversation unless it is necessary.</p>

            <h2 id="sharing">When information is shared</h2>
            <p>Information you choose to publish—such as profile details, housing posts, marketplace listings, helper services, reviews, and photos—may be visible to other users. Some contact details may be disclosed only after a relevant match or accepted request, depending on the feature.</p>
            <p>We may share information with service providers that help us run Nestify, when required by law, or when reasonably necessary to protect users, the public, or our rights. We do not sell personal information.</p>

            <h2 id="security">Security and retention</h2>
            <p>We use reasonable safeguards designed to protect information, but no online system can promise complete security. Protect your password and avoid sharing sensitive financial credentials, PINs, or one-time codes.</p>
            <p>We retain information for as long as needed to provide the service, maintain reliable records, resolve disputes, enforce our agreements, or meet legal and security obligations. Backups and audit records may persist for a limited period after deletion.</p>

            <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
            <p>You can review and update much of your account information through your profile. You may ask about access, correction, or deletion of personal information by contacting the Nestify team through the project’s usual support channel. We may need to retain certain records where required for security, fraud prevention, or legal reasons.</p>

            <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p>We may update this Privacy Policy as Nestify evolves. We will revise the “Last updated” date when we do. Your continued use of Nestify after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
